{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0110","billNumberShort":"H.B. 110","billNumberLong":"HB0110S06","fileNumber":"2026FL0504","shortTitle":"Offender Modifications","currentSubVersion":"6","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"CLANCT","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Clancy, Tyler","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCKELMK","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses provisions related to offenders.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>allows a court to order the Division of Adult Probation and Parole to supervise an individual convicted of class B misdemeanors under certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Board of Pardons and Parole (board), if considering whether to parole an offender who has previously been paroled and had the offender's parole revoked due to a new criminal offense, to consider the facts and circumstances of the new criminal offense in determining whether the offender should be paroled again;<hr><ltbullet>allows the board, with certain exceptions, to only consider a pardon for an offender who has committed an offense that requires the offender to register on the Sex, Kidnap, and Child Abuse Offender Registry (the registry) if:<hr><ltbullet1>for a sex offender required to register on the registry for 10 years, 10 years have passed from when the sex offender entered the community after the sex offender's conviction; or<hr><ltbullet1>for a sex offender required to register on the registry for the sex offender's lifetime, 20 years have passed from when the sex offender entered the community after the sex offender's conviction;<hr><ltbullet>does not allow an offender who has committed an offense that requires the offender to register on the registry at the time the offender is sentenced to receive a certificate of eligibility of expungement from the Bureau of Criminal Identification; and<hr><ltbullet>adds to the requirements for the board to meet before the board may parole an offender before the offender's minimum term of imprisonment has been met.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Shad Larson","fiscalAnalyst":"Sean C. Faherty","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"YDXUJOIJIA","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-29 15:01:47.730","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-29 15:01:47.747","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0110","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2025-12-29 15:01:49.927","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for HB0110","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2025-12-29 15:01:49.927","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Clerk of the House","actionDate":"2026-01-14 13:48:08.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for HB0110","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate":"2026-01-19 15:48:25.821","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA3","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note publicly available for HB0110","owner":"